<main>
  <h1>PixelDiT Implementation Guide for SynthaEngine</h1>
  <p><strong>Date:</strong> 2026-06-03</p>
  <p>
    Research target: PixelDiT, Pixel Diffusion Transformers for Image Generation.
    Project page: <a href="https://pixeldit.github.io/">https://pixeldit.github.io/</a>.
    Code: <a href="https://github.com/NVlabs/PixelDiT">https://github.com/NVlabs/PixelDiT</a>.
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    This companion HTMLX file mirrors the implementation guide in a browser-readable
    form and includes code blocks for workflow payloads, schema sketches, and command
    examples. It is documentation only; no application source files were changed.
  </div>

  <h2>Executive Summary</h2>
  <p>
    PixelDiT is a VAE-free pixel-space diffusion transformer. It generates directly
    in RGB pixel space using a dual-level transformer architecture: a patch-level
    pathway for global semantics and a pixel-level pathway for texture refinement.
  </p>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Question</th><th>Answer</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Official NVIDIA code?</td><td>Yes, in <code>NVlabs/PixelDiT</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Hugging Face weights?</td><td>Yes, ImageNet and T2I model repos exist.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Official Hugging Face Diffusers pipeline?</td><td>No current first-class <code>PixelDiT*Pipeline</code> support found.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Local RTX 3060 12 GB?</td><td>Possible for constrained experiments, not comfortable for 1024px production or training.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Recommended SynthaEngine path?</td><td>Custom <code>pixeldit</code> workflow family with subprocess isolation.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>What PixelDiT Is</h2>
  <p>
    PixelDiT removes the VAE bottleneck used by latent diffusion systems. Instead
    of denoising compressed latents and decoding through a VAE, it denoises pixels
    directly. This can preserve high-frequency details such as text and texture, but
    it increases activation pressure at higher resolutions.
  </p>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Architecture part</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Patch-level DiT pathway</td><td>Global layout, semantics, prompt alignment.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Pixel-level DiT pathway</td><td>Dense local detail and texture refinement.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Pixel-wise AdaLN</td><td>Per-pixel modulation from semantic tokens.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Pixel token compaction</td><td>Reduces dense attention cost without a VAE.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>FlowDPM solver</td><td>Official inference sampler style.</td></tr>
  </table>
  <pre><code class="language-text">prompt
  -> Gemma-2 text encoder
  -> patch-level MM-DiT semantic pathway
  -> semantic tokens + timestep
  -> pixel-wise AdaLN conditioning
  -> pixel-level transformer refinement
  -> RGB pixel output</code></pre>

  <h2>Modalities And Sub-Pipelines</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Modality</th><th>Availability</th><th>SynthaEngine recommendation</th></tr>
    <tr><td>ImageNet class-to-image</td><td>Available in <code>c2i/</code>.</td><td>Optional <code>pixeldit.class2img</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Text-to-image</td><td>Available in <code>t2i/</code>.</td><td>Initial <code>pixeldit.text2img</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>FlowEdit image editing</td><td>Research/demo direction.</td><td>Do not expose until stable code and contract exist.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Img2img</td><td>No official standalone pipeline.</td><td>Do not expose initially.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Inpaint</td><td>No official standalone pipeline.</td><td>Do not expose initially.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>ControlNet</td><td>No official PixelDiT ControlNet pipeline.</td><td>Do not expose initially.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>IP-Adapter</td><td>Not part of official contract.</td><td>Do not expose initially.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Video</td><td>Not available.</td><td>Out of scope.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Diffusers Support Check</h2>
  <p>
    Current evidence shows no official PixelDiT pipeline in Hugging Face Diffusers.
    NVIDIA PixelDiT depends on Diffusers in its requirements, but its model and
    sampler code live in custom PixelDiT modules such as <code>pixdit_core</code>,
    <code>c2i</code>, and <code>t2i</code>.
  </p>
  <pre><code class="language-powershell">.venv\Scripts\python.exe -c "import diffusers; print(diffusers.__version__); print(any('PixelDiT' in name or 'PixDiT' in name for name in dir(diffusers)))"</code></pre>
  <p>Observed locally in SynthaEngine: Diffusers <code>0.38.0</code>, PixelDiT symbol check <code>False</code>.</p>

  <h2>Local Feasibility: Yes And No</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Path</th><th>Verdict</th><th>Details</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Yes: local proof-of-concept</td><td>Feasible to attempt</td><td>Use 256px or 512px, batch 1, one image, 25-50 steps, subprocess execution, and careful cleanup.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>No: local production/training</td><td>Not realistic</td><td>Do not promise 1024px T2I, batching, 50K evaluation, or training on RTX 3060 12 GB.</td></tr>
  </table>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{
  "task_type": "pixeldit.text2img",
  "defaults": {
    "width": 512,
    "height": 512,
    "steps": 25,
    "cfg_scale": 2.75,
    "num_images": 1,
    "sampling_algo": "flow_dpm-solver",
    "interval_guidance": [0.0, 1.0],
    "memory_preset": "subprocess_low_vram",
    "precision": "bf16",
    "quantization": "none",
    "experimental_ack": true
  }
}</code></pre>

  <h2>Quantization Options</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Option</th><th>Possible?</th><th>Recommendation</th></tr>
    <tr><td>BF16 / FP16</td><td>Yes</td><td>Use first. Try BF16, fall back to FP16 if needed.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CPU offload / staged load</td><td>Yes with wrapper work</td><td>Recommended before quantization.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Text encoder bitsandbytes</td><td>Maybe</td><td>Experimental; depends on Windows support and code changes.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Diffusers pipeline quantization</td><td>No direct path</td><td>Requires official or custom Diffusers pipeline components.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>GGUF</td><td>No direct path</td><td>Requires model conversion and compatible model class.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>torchao / quanto</td><td>Maybe</td><td>Future manual model-level optimization.</td></tr>
  </table>
  <pre><code class="language-python">PixelDiTQuantization = Literal[
    "none",
    "text_encoder_bnb_8bit",
    "text_encoder_bnb_4bit",
    "model_torchao_int8_experimental",
    "model_quanto_int8_experimental"
]</code></pre>

  <h2>Cloud Options</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Provider</th><th>Use case</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
    <tr><td>RunPod</td><td>Custom Docker experiments</td><td>Good for RTX 4090, A6000, A100, H100, H200 style pods.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Lambda Cloud</td><td>Managed GPU VMs</td><td>Good for A6000, A100, H100, B200 options.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Vast.ai</td><td>Lower-cost marketplace</td><td>Best for interruptible or budget experiments after checking host reliability.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Hugging Face Inference Endpoints</td><td>Managed private serving</td><td>Use a custom container; PixelDiT is not currently deployed by default providers.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>AWS/GCP/Azure</td><td>Enterprise controls</td><td>More expensive, useful for compliance and private networking.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>SynthaEngine Implementation Plan</h2>
  <p>Add PixelDiT as a new model family and workflow task.</p>
  <pre><code class="language-text">backend/pixeldit/__init__.py
backend/pixeldit/pipeline.py
backend/pixeldit/subprocess_runner.py
backend/pixeldit/subprocess_io.py
backend/workflow/pixeldit.py
frontend/pixeldit/text2img.html
frontend/pixeldit/text2img.js
testing/test_pixeldit_workflow.py
testing/test_pixeldit_subprocess.py
testing/test_frontend_pixeldit_scripts.py</code></pre>

  <h3>Workflow Schema Sketch</h3>
  <pre><code class="language-python">class PixelDiTText2ImgInputs(BaseModel):
    prompt: str = ""
    negative_prompt: str = "low quality, worst quality, over-saturated, blurry, deformed, watermark"
    steps: int = Field(default=25, ge=1, le=100)
    cfg_scale: float = Field(default=2.75, ge=0.0, le=30.0)
    width: int = Field(default=512, ge=256, le=1536)
    height: int = Field(default=512, ge=256, le=1536)
    seed: int | None = None
    model: str | None = None
    model_path: str | None = None
    config: str = "t2i/configs/PixelDiT_1024px_pixel_diffusion_stage3.yaml"
    num_images: int = Field(default=1, ge=1, le=1)
    sampling_algo: Literal["flow_dpm-solver"] = "flow_dpm-solver"
    interval_guidance: tuple[float, float] = (0.0, 1.0)
    precision: Literal["bf16", "fp16", "fp32"] = "bf16"
    memory_preset: Literal["subprocess_low_vram", "subprocess_standard"] = "subprocess_low_vram"
    quantization: Literal["none", "text_encoder_bnb_8bit", "text_encoder_bnb_4bit"] = "none"
    experimental_ack: bool = True
    batch_id: str | None = None</code></pre>

  <h3>Workflow Payload</h3>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{
  "kind": "workflow",
  "payload": {
    "tasks": [
      {
        "id": "t1",
        "type": "pixeldit.text2img",
        "inputs": {
          "prompt": "a quiet glass greenhouse at sunrise, detailed plants, soft mist",
          "negative_prompt": "low quality, blurry, watermark",
          "width": 512,
          "height": 512,
          "steps": 25,
          "cfg_scale": 2.75,
          "seed": 2026,
          "memory_preset": "subprocess_low_vram",
          "experimental_ack": true
        }
      }
    ],
    "return": "@t1.images"
  }
}</code></pre>

  <h3>Subprocess Wrapper Sketch</h3>
  <pre><code class="language-python">def generate_text2img(params: dict[str, object]) -> dict[str, list[str]]:
    return run_pixeldit_subprocess("text2img", params)


def run_pixeldit_subprocess(operation: str, params: dict[str, object]) -> dict[str, list[str]]:
    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix="pixeldit_") as tmpdir:
        input_path = Path(tmpdir) / "input.json"
        output_path = Path(tmpdir) / "output.json"
        input_path.write_text(json.dumps({"operation": operation, "params": params}))
        completed = subprocess.run(
            [sys.executable, "-m", "backend.pixeldit.subprocess_runner", str(input_path), str(output_path)],
            cwd=str(REPO_ROOT),
        )
        payload = json.loads(output_path.read_text())
        if completed.returncode != 0 or not payload.get("ok"):
            raise RuntimeError(f"PixelDiT subprocess failed: {payload.get('error')}")
        return payload["result"]</code></pre>

  <h2>Official Command Example</h2>
  <pre><code class="language-bash">cd t2i/
python inference.py \
  --config configs/PixelDiT_1024px_pixel_diffusion_stage3.yaml \
  --model_path pixeldit_t2i_v1.pth \
  --txt_file prompts.txt \
  --custom_height 512 --custom_width 512 \
  --cfg_scale 2.75 --seed 2026 \
  --step 25 \
  --negative_prompt "low quality, worst quality, over-saturated, blurry, deformed, watermark" \
  --work_dir "."</code></pre>

  <h2>Validation Commands</h2>
  <pre><code class="language-powershell">.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m compileall backend
.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest testing/test_pixeldit_workflow.py -q
.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest testing/test_pixeldit_subprocess.py -q
.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest testing/test_workflow_catalog_capabilities.py -q</code></pre>

  <h2>Recommended First PR Scope</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>pixeldit.text2img</code> only.</li>
    <li>One checkpoint: <code>nvidia/PixelDiT-1300M-1024px</code>.</li>
    <li>512x512 default, batch size 1.</li>
    <li><code>flow_dpm-solver</code> only.</li>
    <li><code>quantization: "none"</code> only.</li>
    <li>No LoRA, ControlNet, IP-Adapter, img2img, inpaint, or training.</li>
    <li>Subprocess execution only.</li>
  </ul>

